- **Workspace manifests** — `[workspace]` + members.

## Non-blocking follow-ups

- **`ScopeId` in vehje-ir** — already landed in R1; BACKLOG
  only notes that any future cross-crate tweak should stay
  reusable.
- **Interned `Str` name expansion** — this round adopts
  `hilavitkutin_str::Str`; follow-up work connects the
  `StringInterner` instance to the compiler driver so the
  runtime-origin bit of `Str` carries real IDs (not just the
  compile-time `str_const!()` path).
- **Incremental resolve for IDE** — delta walk that re-resolves
  only the changed subtree, keyed off AST node diff.

## Diagnostic surface

- `ResolveError` currently carries two variants
  (`UnresolvedIdentifier`, `DuplicateDefinition`); additional
  variants (`AmbiguousImport`, `CycleDetected`, `PrivateAccess`,
  `UnknownCrate`) arrive with the rule that first emits them.
- `ManifestError` currently carries two variants (`Parse`,
  `NotImplemented`); real TOML parsing will extend this with
  `MissingField`, `InvalidVersion`, `DuplicateDependency`, etc.
- The `From<ResolveError> for Diagnostic` conversion currently
  emits static placeholder messages; follow-up rounds replace
  them with per-variant messages once the producer rules land.

## Scheduler handoff for collection fields

The four skeleton-backed collection fields (`Scope::symbols`,
`ScopeTree::scopes`, `Resolved::resolution`,
`Manifest::dependencies`) are tracked in SHAME.md against #131
(vehje-schedule as hilavitkutin WorkUnit home) and #134
(persistence spine). Once the scheduler owns resolver state,
each field moves to a scheduler-managed `Column<T>` or a
`Map<K, V, N: Cap>` descriptor over an AccessSet-typed
read/write pair. Do not rewrite the fields inline before
#131 lands.
